        "inventory_expansion_required": false,
        "proof_strategy": "direct",
        "statement": "Assume Countable Choice and use the scalar and Dirac free-field constructions of [[lem-qft-smeared-free-scalar]] and [[lem-qft-free-dirac-car-locality]] with their current draft hypotheses, including the Dirac projection and CAR inputs in [[lem-qft-dirac-projection-matrices]] and [[lem-qft-fock-ccr-car]]. For a real scalar test $f\\in\\mathcal S(\\mathbb R^4)$, $\\overline{\\Phi_\\mu(f)}=\\sqrt2\\,\\Phi_{\\rm Segal}(K_\\mu f)$ is self-adjoint on the exact domain given by [[lem-qft-segal-weyl-domain]]. On scalar bosonic Fock space, $N_s=d\\Gamma(1)$, $H_s=d\\Gamma(\\omega_\\mu)$, and $P_{s,j}=d\\Gamma(-k_j)$ are the maximal real multipliers of [[lem-qft-second-quantized-spectrum]]; in particular,\n$$D(N_s)=\\left\\{\\Psi=(\\Psi_n):\\sum_{n\\ge1}n^2\\|\\Psi_n\\|^2<\\infty\\right\\},$$\nand the Hamiltonian and momentum domains are exactly the square-integrability domains of the sums of their one-particle multipliers.\n\nOn the specified Dirac Fock space, spacetime-smeared fields $\\Psi(F)$ are bounded, while the translation generators $H_D,P_{D,j}$ have the exact maximal domains and joint PVM stated in [[lem-qft-dirac-fermionic-translation-spectrum]]. For any one of these self-adjoint real-multiplier operators $A$, a normalized $\\Psi\\in D(A)$ has finite mean $\\langle\\Psi,A\\Psi\\rangle$ and finite variance\n$$\\operatorname{Var}_\\Psi(A)=\\|(A-\\langle\\Psi,A\\Psi\\rangle)\\Psi\\|^2.$$\nMembership in $D(A)$ suffices for finite variance and does not require $\\Psi\\in D(A^2)$. A product $AB\\Psi$ is defined only when $\\Psi\\in D(B)$ and $B\\Psi\\in D(A)$, as specified in [[lem-nrqm-uncertainty-schrodinger-robertson-anticommutator-bound]].\n\nFor the scalar field, smooth spacetime tests approximating a point mass produce vacuum vectors with norms diverging to infinity. For the equal-time Dirac CAR field, spatial tests approximating a point mass produce bounded smeared operators whose operator norms diverge. Thus neither construction gives a point-field value in the indicated norm topology. The supplied free-field results define only smeared fields and do not define coincident diagonal products.",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "literature-derived",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "David Tong, Quantum Field Theory, author-hosted complete lecture notes, Chapter 2, §§2.2 and 2.7",
              "url": "https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/qft/qfthtml/S2.html",
              "locator": "Complete HTML Chapter 2; bosonic Fock sectors and number operator, the formal point-field warning, and free scalar two-point function, equations 2.123–2.127 and 2.165–2.170."
